CORE
access.c
--function f --pointer-check
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[precondition_instance\.1\] .*static array parameter x must provide access to its declared minimum: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The --function harness sizes the argument array by the earlier argument n, so
the last element promised by the runtime static minimum is accessible.
